{"title": "Why Charts Jump", "type": "Technical lesson", "hooks": ["Why do charts sometimes jump, with nothing in between?", "Nobody tells you which gaps fill. Volume does.", "A gap can run or fade. One clue tells them apart."], "scenes": [{"kind": "hook", "vo": "Nobody tells you which gaps fill. Volume does.", "text": "Why charts jump", "chart": null}, {"kind": "big", "text": "A gap: no trades between", "vo": "That's a gap. The price opened far from the last close, with no trades in between. News or earnings often cause it.", "chart": null}, {"kind": "cards", "head": "Two kinds of gap", "vo": "Some gap and go, and keep running on strong volume. Others fade back and fill the gap.", "items": [{"text": "Gap and go", "sub": "keeps running on strong volume", "icon": "up"}, {"text": "Gap and fill", "sub": "fades back towards the close", "icon": "down"}], "cues": [{"say": "gap and go", "do": "item", "i": 0}, {"say": "fill the gap", "do": "item", "i": 1}], "chart": null}, {"kind": "big", "text": "Volume is the clue", "vo": "Volume after the gap is often the best clue. The same clue works on any jump through a level.", "chart": null}, {"kind": "question", "chart": 0, "badge": "Q1", "head": "Real or fake?", "vo": "Here, the price just closed above the last 20 candles' high. Real breakout, or fake?", "win": [20, 115], "options": ["Real: it keeps going", "Fake: it falls back inside the range"], "answer": 1, "show": 90, "cues": [{"say": "", "do": "options"}, {"say": "", "do": "line", "price": 120.55, "label": "20-candle high", "tone": "trigger"}]}, {"kind": "answer", "chart": 0, "head": "Fake, on weak volume", "vo": "Fake. It closed back inside the range within six candles. Volume on the break was only 0.7 times average.", "win": [20, 115], "reveal_to": 115, "carry": true, "cues": []}, {"kind": "outro", "text": "Practise trading the gaps", "vo": "Meme Street has earnings every couple of days. Practise trading the gaps at memestreet.net.", "chart": null}], "caption": "Why do cha